[ ] Make add honor --workspace as an exact write target =add-workspace-target $Found 2026-10-12. add treats --workspace as a read filter, which is wrong for a write. (1) Without --charter or --file it is ignored: resolve_acts_target falls back to the primary workspace, so 'clearhead add --workspace clearhead-core action x' and even '--workspace nope' both write to the platform root next.actions, silently. (2) With --charter it narrows the search by case-insensitive substring (workspace_dirs uses contains), so '--workspace clearhead' matches clearhead-core, clearhead-cli and clearhead.nvim and the first charter match wins. Expected: an exact name that picks the write target, an error when it names no workspace, and an error when it matches more than one. Same check likely applies to add charter and add plan.$ !2 +bug,cli ^2026-10-12T00:42 #01a12d8f-6eeb-74f2-9a4b-ffad237e4126
